1
00:02:31,067 --> 00:02:41,067
All pirates searching for the treasure of One Piece must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

2
00:02:41,067 --> 00:02:46,067
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

3
00:02:46,067 --> 00:02:52,067
Gold Roger and his crew were the only men to ever chart these waters and learn all the secrets they held.

4
00:02:52,067 --> 00:03:00,067
For the rest of the pirates of the world, this has proven to be the end of the road, a graveyard of dreams.

5
00:03:00,067 --> 00:03:09,067
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber after eating the gum gum fruit, set sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

6
00:03:09,067 --> 00:03:13,067
I'm gonna be the king of the pirates!

7
00:03:17,067 --> 00:03:24,067
Two years have passed since the War of the Best in Marineford. Luffy and his crew reunite to continue on to the New World.

8
00:03:24,067 --> 00:03:30,067
The first stop on their journey is Fishman Island, which resides thousands of feet below sea level.

9
00:03:30,067 --> 00:03:35,067
Now, they're separated once again, stirring up trouble all over the ocean floor.

10
00:03:35,067 --> 00:03:40,067
Luffy smuggled the Princess Shirahoshi out of Ryugu Palace for an adventure.

11
00:03:40,067 --> 00:03:45,067
Robin received a lead on the whereabouts of a pony glyph hidden on Fishman Island.

12
00:03:45,067 --> 00:03:51,067
The crew can take care of themselves. I can't miss a chance to uncover the world's lost history.

13
00:03:51,067 --> 00:03:56,067
Frankie stumbled upon the sunny at the sea forest, a resting place for sunken ships.

14
00:03:58,067 --> 00:04:02,067
I'll do the ship coding for you. And I'll do it with gusto.

15
00:04:02,067 --> 00:04:07,067
Hmm. Haven't heard that one in a while. Oh, uh, sorry. I never caught your name.

16
00:04:07,067 --> 00:04:09,067
Call me Den.

17
00:04:09,067 --> 00:04:15,067
By the way, I've been meaning to ask you. There's a dude sitting all alone over there. Do you know who he is?

18
